1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,610
(Được chép bởi TurboScribe. Nâng cấp lên Không giới hạn để gỡ bỏ thông báo này.) Welcome to ARC Office Hours. Let's dive right into this explainer.

2
00:00:04,130 --> 00:00:08,750
Today, we're talking about DeFi Recipes – Safer DeFi Automation on ARC.

3
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:13,090
As we go through this, we're going to keep it laser-focused on three core pillars.

4
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:15,850
First, taking a security-first approach.

5
00:00:16,310 --> 00:00:18,610
Second, enabling automated strategies.

6
00:00:19,170 --> 00:00:23,070
And third, unpacking exactly why all of this is built on ARC.

7
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:26,090
Automate DeFi. Keep Control.

8
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:28,310
Section 01. The Problem.

9
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:31,270
DeFi is powerful, but automation is risky.

10
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:33,830
Listen, the more we automate things,

11
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:37,210
the more absolutely crucial those underlying guardrails become.

12
00:00:37,530 --> 00:00:40,610
There are four major bottlenecks we're facing right now.

13
00:00:40,910 --> 00:00:43,330
First, there are just way too many manual steps.

14
00:00:43,630 --> 00:00:45,650
You're forced to string together multiple transactions

15
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:48,590
across completely different protocols just to pull off one strategy.

16
00:00:48,970 --> 00:00:50,850
Second, smart contract risk.

17
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:53,790
Automation without strict guardrails can take a tiny mistake

18
00:00:53,790 --> 00:00:57,030
or an unexpected contract behavior and literally magnify it.

19
00:00:57,330 --> 00:00:59,070
Third, setting the wrong parameters.

20
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,210
Misconfiguring a protocol, a specific token, a function,

21
00:01:02,330 --> 00:01:05,570
or allowable slippage amounts can be an absolute disaster for your wallet.

22
00:01:05,950 --> 00:01:07,850
And fourth, it's just hard for normal users.

23
00:01:08,230 --> 00:01:12,330
These powerful workflows are simply still too hard for regular folks to operate safely.

24
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:15,370
Which brings us to Section 02. The Solution.

25
00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:16,730
DeFi Recipes.

26
00:01:17,310 --> 00:01:18,450
Create a strategy once.

27
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:19,890
Configure its boundaries.

28
00:01:20,450 --> 00:01:21,510
Automate with control.

29
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:24,030
Here's how that actual flow works.

30
00:01:24,570 --> 00:01:29,130
First, you create, actively choosing a strategy that fits your financial goals.

31
00:01:29,490 --> 00:01:35,130
Then, you configure it, setting strict parameters to define exactly what it can and can't do.

32
00:01:35,610 --> 00:01:40,510
Next, you automate, letting the system execute those steps for you automatically.

33
00:01:41,030 --> 00:01:44,850
And finally, you monitor, keeping clear track of what happens

34
00:01:44,850 --> 00:01:48,190
so you know everything is running smoothly within your set boundaries.

35
00:01:49,090 --> 00:01:51,630
Automation should not have unlimited permissions.

36
00:01:51,970 --> 00:01:55,390
Because we firmly believe that we don't want unlimited permissions,

37
00:01:55,890 --> 00:01:57,110
the golden rule is this.

38
00:01:57,730 --> 00:02:00,730
Every single recipe has clear, controlled boundaries.

39
00:02:01,110 --> 00:02:03,810
It only does exactly what you've permitted it to do.

40
00:02:04,370 --> 00:02:06,930
Moving into Section 03. Security.

41
00:02:07,410 --> 00:02:08,410
Security first.

42
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:12,350
We evaluate whether a protocol is safe enough to automate in the first place,

43
00:02:12,630 --> 00:02:15,270
rather than just optimizing for APY alone.

44
00:02:15,810 --> 00:02:19,250
To figure that out objectively, we use a protocol score.

45
00:02:19,630 --> 00:02:22,530
This gives us a structured signal to determine whether a protocol

46
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:24,250
should even be eligible for automation.

47
00:02:24,790 --> 00:02:26,030
We look at four specific things.

48
00:02:26,410 --> 00:02:27,710
First up, security maturity.

49
00:02:28,070 --> 00:02:29,570
How battle-tested is the protocol?

50
00:02:29,950 --> 00:02:31,170
Second, audit coverage.

51
00:02:31,350 --> 00:02:33,870
How extensive and rigorous have their security reviews been?

52
00:02:34,290 --> 00:02:37,210
Third, we look at their incident history, to see if they've had breaches.

53
00:02:37,590 --> 00:02:38,830
And fourth, response quality.

54
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:41,970
If something did go wrong, how well did the team actually handle it?

55
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:46,410
So at the end of the day, guardrails are greater than unlimited access.

56
00:02:47,110 --> 00:02:49,490
Let's jump to Section 04. Live Demo.

57
00:02:49,690 --> 00:02:50,990
From recipe to execution.

58
00:02:51,470 --> 00:02:54,910
We're going to keep our focus entirely on the actual user journey here,

59
00:02:55,130 --> 00:02:56,850
rather than every little UI detail.

60
00:02:57,370 --> 00:02:59,170
The journey takes five easy steps.

61
00:02:59,490 --> 00:03:00,970
Step 1. You choose a recipe,

62
